type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

\whitespace trim

A web font manager for TiddlyWiki. Drop a font file (`.woff2`, `.woff`, `.ttf`, `.otf`) onto the wiki: it is turned into a self-contained stylesheet tiddler (`$:/fonts/<Name>`, tagged ''$:/tags/Stylesheet'') holding a &nbsp;`@font-face`&nbsp; rule with the font embedded in base64 — no network request, works offline and in single-file wikis.

! Usage

Drag a font file onto the wiki and import it from the usual import screen. Once imported, the typeface is available to any CSS in the wiki. Reference it by name with &nbsp;`font-family`&nbsp;, e.g. in a stylesheet tiddler:

```css
.tc-tiddler-title { font-family: "Lobster"; }
```

Or inline in wikitext:

```
@@font-family:"Caveat Brush";Some fancy text@@
```

The plugin itself ships no font. Fonts larger than about 300 KB get a note: prefer WOFF2, which is much lighter.
